.SH "NAME"
probe::syscall_any \- Record entry into a syscall
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.nf
probe syscall_any {}
.fi
.SH "VALUES"
.PP
\fIname\fR
.RS 4
name of the syscall
.RE
.PP
\fIsyscall_nr\fR
.RS 4
number of the syscall
.RE
.SH "CONTEXT"
.PP
The process performing the syscall
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
Prefers kernel\&.tracepoint(\(lqsys_enter\(rq) when vmlinux\&.h BTF tracepoints are available; falls back to kernel\&.trace(\(lqsys_enter\(rq) (kernel 3\&.5+)\&.
.SH SEE ALSO\n 
.IR tapset::syscall_any (3stap)
